Hey, if you are going to have a mall level then you need mall security
guards (instead of Kops) on that level only.  Also - no pets allowed in
shops.  And - there should be a food court, but you have to wear some kind of
armor *and* shoes/boots (no shirt, no shoes, - no service ;^) to get
in.  If you get in a fight with a store owner or steal something the
security gaurds will attack you en-masse.  They should be *very* dangerous
- ie carry wands of magic missile which they use against you with the
same frequency as a dragon's breath attack.  Attacking one guard would
cause all of his buddies to come to his rescue ala Kops.  Even a ring of
conflict should not help against mall security.

In other words, a mall level should be *very* dangerous to try to
steal from.

Also, prices should be much higher in the mall than elsewhere - about
double their normal price (but when you sell items you still get the
same cheap amount).

It should be like a maze level with lots of rooms embedded in the maze.
There should be lots of other humans roaming around in the maze and
wandering in-and-out of shops.  These humans, if you do a "/" on them,
will be reported as "consumers".  They have money but are unarmed and
will not fight, only yell a lot.  If you attack one of them he will start
yelling at you.  Then a security guard will show up and drag you away
to the stairwell and throw you down it.  If you put on a ring of conflict
while in a room full of consumers they will all start yelling at each
other.  Then a guard will show up and tell all the consumers to calm down,
then instruct you that wearing a ring of conflict is very antisocial and
against the mall rules - take it off or leave.  If you don't take it off
then down the stairs you go.

There should be pickpockets and shoplifters as well as consumers.  Killing
either of these will not get you in trouble.  But they are all "@"s.

Consumers should pick up items in shops and buy them while you are in the
shop.  So you have no guarantee that items will stay in shops - and while
you can kill and rob a consumer as he exits a shop - you will get kicked
out of the mall for doing it.

Some shops to think about including -

o jewelry store (rings, amulets, jewels, stones.)

o blacksmith (for a price he will sharpen and rustproof weapons with
  '-'s - but you will have to leave it with him for a few hundred turns.
  Perhaps a mail daemon could bring you news that your weapon is finished.
  Same goes for armor.)

o Magician (provides certain special services such as improving your stats
  - along with derogatory comments about your current stats.  Very expensive
  and should only offer selected services out of a large menu - selections
  allowed are picked when the shop is created).  Props - like blindfolds and
  crystal balls.

o Hairdressers - mirrors - along with pushy attendent who knows just how to
  improve your image.  Allowing her to do your hair will temporarilly increase
  your charisma ;^).

o Spa - increase your strength by working out ;^).  Lift weights until you
  are fainting.  Then eat the protein rations they sell.  Gain a point.  If
  you sign up for the full program (out of ignorance - ;^) the attendent
  will strap wrist- and ankle-weights on you, which if worn long enough
  will raise your strength, but the effect is like a scroll of punishment.
  You need remove curse to get rid of them.

o Martial arts studio - increase your dexterity, stealth, by studying martial
  arts.  You have to leave your weapons and armor in the corner and fight the
  teacher hand-to-hand.  He won't kill you, but he will knock your hit points
  down until you think you are going to die ;^).  Then your stats will have
  increased slightly after you recover.  There should be shuriken and other
  similar weapons for sale.  The teacher will prevent consumers from taking
  your stuff, but you wouldn't necessarilly know that the first time you
  try this shop ;^).

Apply for a credit card at the information booth.  The mail daemon will
deliver it to you a few hundred turns later.  Perhaps credit-fraud would
be the only relatively safe way to rip off a mall shop.  And you couldn't
get away with it twice - the next shop you show the card to will confiscate
it - it's on the list.  And if you apply for another card - sorry - your
credit is denied.  Unless, of course, you feel like a new man...

